; The orphan.  Its apex names ns.example. as its name server, the same
; name the parent's referral names, and then gives no address for it.
;
; On the Internet this is what rand.orphan.e-ontap.com is: the address
; of the name server lives in the parent as glue and nowhere else, so
; the only way to reach the zone is to have kept what the referral said.
; A resolver which discards it in favour of the authoritative NS RRset
; -- the same names, higher ranking -- has to look ns.example. up, and
; the only server which could answer is the one it is trying to reach.
$ORIGIN example.
$TTL 3600
@	IN	SOA	ns.example. root.example. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@	IN	NS	ns.example.
www	IN	A	192.0.2.1
